#---
# purpose: "A spec over an untyped clause is documentation at a call whose argument is not known to be in its domain: a float held as any comes back as that float"
# oracle: oracle.exs
# oracle.stamp: f111859363b73a1b
#---
#
# `f/1` is specified over integers but its clause has no test, so it admits a
# float. The caller holds the argument as `any`, so the call's result is read
# from what the clause returns, not from the spec.
@spec f(integer) :: integer
def f(x), do: x

def main() do
  send(self(), 1.5)

  receive do
    x -> dbg(f(x))
  end
end
